FT_c pins are dedicated USB Type-C CC pins (**PB4** / `UCPD1_CC2` and **PB6** / `UCPD1_CC1`) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.70, p.72]. To safely use an FT_c pin (e.g., PB4) as a 5 V input:

1. **Disable the Dead-Battery Pull-Down Resistors (`PWR_CR3_UCPD_DBDIS`):**
   At reset, internal dead-battery pull-down resistors ($5.1\,\text{k}\Omega$) on PB4 and PB6 are active by default [STM32G474_Datasheet p.72, STM32G474_RM0440 p.255]. You must enable the PWR clock and set `PWR_CR3_UCPD_DBDIS` in `PWR->CR3` to disable them.
2. **Disable Internal Pull-Up and Pull-Down Resistors (`GPIOx_PUPDR = 00b`):**
   Per Table 17 Note 3: when $V_{\text{IN}} > \min(V_{\mathrm{DD}}, V_{\mathrm{DDA}}) + 0.3\,\text{V}$, the internal pull-up and pull-down resistors must be disabled [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84]. Configure the pin in floating mode (`PUPDR = 00b`).
3. **Configure GPIO Direction as Input (`GPIOx_MODER = 00b`):**
   Set the pin to input mode in `MODER`.

---

